["You can collect all the "zeroth" (input[0].previous_output.txid) ancestors by repeatedly fetching the parent transaction and following its input[0] until there are no more inputs (or until a safety depth limit). The function below keeps the existing signature and returns a JSON object with an array of parent txids under "DATA".

Notes: it uses Electrum's "blockchain.transaction.get" (like your original), stops when a transaction has no inputs, and uses a depth limit to avoid infinite loops. Adjust the collected value (txid strings, full hex, or decoded transaction fields) as you prefer.

```rust
fn auth_base(authbase: String, tx: &String) -> Result<Json<Value>, ECerror> {
    let client = Client::new("tcp://localhost:50001")?;
    let method = "blockchain.transaction.get";

    // fetch initial tx hex
    let params = vec![Param::String(tx.to_string())];
    let mut electr_tx_res = ElectrumApi::raw_call(&client, &method, params)?;
    let mut tx_hex = electr_tx_res.as_str().unwrap_or("").to_string();

    let mut zeroth_txs: Vec<String> = Vec::new();
    let mut depth = 0usize;
    let max_depth = 1000usize; // safety limit

    while !tx_hex.is_empty() && depth < max_depth {
        // decode the current transaction
        let decoded = decode_transaction(&tx_hex).unwrap();

        // stop if there are no inputs (coinbase or no parents)
        if decoded.input.is_empty() {
            break;
        }

        // get the parent txid (input[0].previous_output.txid)
        let parent_txid = zeroth_index(decoded.clone())?;
        let parent_txid_str = parent_txid.to_string();

        // add parent txid to the result array
        zeroth_txs.push(parent_txid_str.clone());

        // fetch parent transaction hex for the next iteration
        let params = vec![Param::String(parent_txid_str)];
        let parent_res = ElectrumApi::raw_call(&client, &method, params)?;
        let parent_hex = parent_res.as_str().unwrap_or("").to_string();

        if parent_hex.is_empty() {
            break;
        }

        tx_hex = parent_hex;
        depth += 1;
    }

    Ok(Json(json!({ "DATA": zeroth_txs })))
}
```

If you prefer to return full transaction hexes or decoded objects instead of txid strings, replace the push to zeroth_txs with the desired values (e.g., push parent_hex or json!(decoded) into a Vec<Value> and return that)."]

